## Why This Is Asked

Assesses end-to-end real-time ingestion, deduplication guarantees, and exactly-once semantics across regional boundaries. Tests Dataflow configuration (watermarks, lateness), BigQuery writes with insertId, and robust monitoring.

## Key Concepts

- Dataflow streaming and Pub/Sub in multi-region setups
- Stateful deduplication by event_id
- BigQuery insertId for idempotent sinks
- Watermarking and allowed lateness
- Cloud Monitoring alerts and incident wiring
- IAM least privilege and service accounts

## Code Example

```java
class DedupDoFn extends DoFn<Event, Event> {
  @StateId("seen") private final StateSpec<ValueState<Boolean>> seen = null;
  @ProcessElement
  public void process(@Element Event e, @StateId("seen") ValueState<Boolean> seen) {
    if (Boolean.FALSE.equals(seen.read())) {
      seen.write(true);
      out.output(e);
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test idempotence and backpressure under traffic spikes?
- What monitoring dashboards would you set up for latency and data-lag, and how would you handle alert fatigue?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of real-time data ingestion on GCP, basic data validation, idempotency via insertId, and integration between Pub/Sub and BigQuery using a simple Cloud Function. Emphasizes low-ops design, immutable inserts, and basic testing.

## Key Concepts

- Pub/Sub triggers and message acknowledgement
- JSON validation and field presence
- De-duplication strategy with insertId
- BigQuery streaming inserts and insertId semantics
- Minimal IAM roles and test planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Cloud Function skeleton (Node.js)
const {BigQuery} = require('@google-cloud/bigquery');
const crypto = require('crypto');
const bigquery = new BigQuery();

exports.incomingLogs = async (message, context) => {
  let data;
  try {
    data = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(message.data, 'base64').toString());
  } catch (e) {
    console.error('Invalid JSON');
    return;
  }
  const required = ['service','level','timestamp','message'];
  if (!required.every(k => data.hasOwnProperty(k))) {
    console.error('Missing fields');
    return;
  }
  const sign = data.service + data.timestamp + data.message;
  const insertId = crypto.createHash('md5').update(sign).digest('hex');
  const row = {
    insertId,
    service: data.service,
    level: data.level,
    timestamp: data.timestamp,
    message: data.message
  };
  await bigquery.dataset('analytics').table('logs').insert(row);
};
```

